/* book exam traps: Using one extent ξ for two independent reactions. Each independent reaction needs its own ξⱼ; otherwise the mole balances conflict. | Taking conversion as ξ divided by total moles. Conversion is (nᵢ₀ − nᵢ)/nᵢ₀, that is ξ scaled by |νᵢ| and divided by the initial moles of that species. | Dropping the sign of νᵢ. A reactant has νᵢ < 0; a positive νᵢ with positive ξ increases that species. | Forgetting inerts. They have νᵢ = 0, stay constant, but appear in nT and in nT₀. | Doubling every coefficient without changing ξ. The reaction is scaled, so ξ must halve for the same physical change. */
